            <ArticleTitle>Distinctive presentation of a diaphragmatic hernia 15 years after a traumatic insult.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>651-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2008.12.057</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diaphragmatic hernias are well-known sequelae of abdominal and chest wall trauma. However, they may go undiagnosed in the acute setting but present later due to gastrointestinal or respiratory complications. A distinctive presentation of a diaphragmatic hernia 15 years after a traumatic insult is herein described. Management strategies are also discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
